# Cockpit (Cursor + cross-vendor)

Operator runs 10–20 parallel Ghostty tabs. Cockpit = **steer without asking**.

## Cursor-specific

- **Statusline:** `~/.cursor/cli-config.json` → `statusLine.command` = `/Users/alien/Projects/agent-infra/scripts/cursor-statusline.sh`
- **Intervals:** `updateIntervalMs: 5000`, `timeoutMs: 3000` — keep script under 3s.
- **Marker:** `◇` on line 1 distinguishes Cursor from Claude `◐`.
- **State files:** same `/tmp/claude-tab-*` and `claude-agent-$PPID` as Claude (PPID = agent process).
- **No cost in Cursor HUD** yet (`—` in agent state); context % + fleet aggregate still work.

## All vendors

| Vendor | HUD | Tab title |
|--------|-----|-----------|
| Claude | 2-line via `~/.claude/statusline.sh` | OSC 2 in statusline |
| Cursor | 2-line via `cursor-statusline.sh` | OSC 2 in statusline |
| Codex | none | `codex-tab-title.sh` + shim flush only |

Shared: `scripts/cockpit_common.sh`. Full doc: `cockpit.md`.

## Editing checklist

1. Change `scripts/` canonical copy; sync `~/.codex/hooks/codex-tab-title.sh` if needed.
2. Use `realpath` for `COCKPIT_DIR` when script may be symlinked.
3. Codex hooks: `COCKPIT_AGENT_PID` from shim, never hook `$PPID`.
4. Line 2 = steering only (loop, compact, git, fleet, others, ⚑) — no throughput/cache noise.
5. Test: `echo '<statusline json>' | ~/.claude/statusline.sh` and `scripts/fleet.sh`.

## Key /tmp paths

`claude-agent-$pid`, `claude-tab-tool-$pid`, `claude-tab-state-$pid`, `cockpit-tab-pending-$pid` (Codex flush), `hutter-fleet-cache` (hutter project only).
